// ../en.md, section 5. These lines carry what the header would have carried.
//
// Twelve scored questions, which is the number in the meta.yaml. The text
// before them is a description and is not scored.
// No standard wording, no control title, no description of a control.
// Controls are addressed by their number.

$CATEGORY: iso-iec-27002

::Note before the following questions::
The following questions cover the way from a treated row in the risk register to
a reasoned number in the statement of applicability. References are by standard,
clause and edition; the wording is to be opened in a licensed copy.

// 1

::The direction::
The number is looked for to fit an intention that comes from the risk treatment,
and not the intention to fit the number.{TRUE
####Right. ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 asks in 6.1.3 for the controls to be determined
from the treatment and only then held against the annex. Anyone turning the
direction around ticks off a list and looks for the risks afterwards.}

// 2

::The clause for the comparison::
In which clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 do the comparison against the annex and
the statement of applicability stand?{
=6.1.3 #Right.
~6.1.2 #That is the risk assessment.
~8.1 #That is carrying it out in operation.
~9.1 #That is evaluating the effectiveness.
####The comparison belongs to planning the treatment and therefore stands in the
same subclause as the treatment itself.}

// 3

::Departing from guidance::
A departure from ISO/IEC 27002\:2022 is a nonconformity.{FALSE
####Wrong. ISO/IEC 27002 is guidance and nobody is certified against it. An
audit holds the organisation against ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 and against its own
determinations.}

// 4

::What belongs to a non-application::
Which two entries belong to a control that is not applied?{
~%50%That it is not applied, entered expressly. #Right.
~%50%A reason that is a finding about the risk situation. #Right.
~%-100%A reason naming the effort the implementation would take. #Effort is a
reason to treat differently and not a statement about the risk.
~%-100%An empty row, because there is nothing to do. #An empty row does not say
whether somebody decided or whether somebody missed it.
####The two together make a non-application a decision. Without the second, what
is really missing is the approved residual risk.}

// 5

::The document at the end::
What is the document called in which it stands, for every number of the annex,
whether it is applied and why?{
=statement of applicability
=the statement of applicability
=Statement of Applicability
####ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 asks for it in 6.1.3. It is built against the annex and
not against the organisation.}

// 6

::An intention with no matching number::
An intention from the treatment fits no number of the annex. What follows?{
=It is a control of your own and stands in the risk register. #Right.
~The treatment is wrong and gets done again. #The annex is no measure for the
treatment.
~The intention is dropped because it does not occur in the annex. #The annex is
a check against what was forgotten and not a closed list.
~It gets put under the nearest number. #Then the reason points at something that
was not meant.
####The annex does not cover every situation. A control of your own is the
ordinary case and not a mistake.}

// 7

::Number range and field::
Assign to each number range of ISO/IEC 27002\:2022 the field it concerns.{
=5 -> organisational
=6 -> people
=7 -> physical
=8 -> technological
####The four ranges are the rough order of the 2022 edition. Which numbers exist
in detail and what stands behind each of them is the subject of a licensed copy.}

// 8

::What the comparison is for::
The comparison against the annex is a check against what was {=forgotten
~counted ~secured ~afforded} and no promise that nothing can happen any
more.{####An organisation can have applied every number and have missed a risk
that occurs in none of them.}

// 9

::The current edition::
Which year is the edition of ISO/IEC 27002 from that this training covers?{#2022:0
####It is rebuilt against the 2013 edition\: the controls are reordered and
carry different numbers.}

// 10

::An older mapping in the house::
A mapping built against the 2013 edition can be carried on unchanged against the
2022 edition.{FALSE
####Wrong. The numbers are assigned anew and some controls have been merged, so
an old number points somewhere else in the new edition.}

// 11

::Order and reasoning::
The comparison is made before the risk treatment. Write in two sentences how
that shows in the finished statement of applicability later.{
####Model answer. The reasons then point at the content of the standard instead
of at a risk row of your own, and they sound the same for every organisation. It
shows in an applied control having no row in the risk register that it points
back to.}

// 12

::Who sets the measure::
What is the reason for a non-application measured against?{
=Against the risk situation of your own organisation. #Right.
~Against the effort the implementation would take. #Effort is a reason to treat
differently.
~Against what is usual in the sector. #Being usual is no finding about your own
risk.
~Against the opinion of the certification body. #It checks; it does not set the
measure.
####The statement of applicability points back at the risk work in both
directions, for application as for non-application.}
